  "notes": "This fixture reads sections 3.4 and 3.5, 4.1, 4.3 to 4.7, 6, 7 and 8. Sections 3.4, 3.5 and 6 are here because table C of docs/capability-coverage.md has rows for them. Section 3.4 is the version declaration, 3.5 the preprocessor, and 6 the statements, with discard, switch and do-while. Section 3.4 gives the version directive, #version. Section 3.5 gives the other preprocessor directives, the operator defined and the predefined macros. Section 3.5 says the version directive is not a preprocessor directive. The fixture lists #version with the preprocessor rows anyway, because table C of docs/capability-coverage.md names it there. The operators of the pp-constant-expression table in section 3.5 have no entries, because section 5.1 gives each of them. The exception is defined, which section 5.1 does not give. It has its entry at 3.5. The #pragma forms STDGL, optimize and debug, and the #extension behaviors require, enable, warn and disable, are arguments of a directive. They are not directives, so they have no entries. The token all of #extension has no entry for the same reason. Section 6 gives the selection statements of 6.2, the iteration statements of 6.3 and the jumps of 6.4, including discard. The compound, declaration and expression statements of section 6 have no keyword, so they have no entries. A compound statement is a group of statements in braces, and a declaration or expression statement ends in a semi-colon. Do-while is one of the thirteen refusals with no rule number (proposal 0059, What the inventory found, item 2). Section 6.1 gives no keyword-led function form, so the statements list has no function entry. Section 4.7 (Order of Qualification) adds no keyword, so it adds no entry. It sets the order of the qualifiers in a declaration. For a variable the order is invariant, interpolation, storage, precision. For a parameter the order is storage, parameter, precision. The identifier location also appears in section 4.3.8.2 for fragment outputs. It has one entry, at 4.3.8.1. Section 4.1.6 makes mat2, mat3 and mat4 aliases of mat2x2, mat3x3 and mat4x4. The 4.1 tables list both spellings, so both have an entry. The keyword layout is the layout-qualifier of section 4.3.8, and it has its own entry, at 4.3.8. The identifiers in its list are not keywords (section 4.3.8), and each has its own entry. Section 7.4 declares the structure gl_DepthRangeParameters and its members near, far and diff. They have no entries. The structure is not a basic type of section 4.1, and its members are fields, not variables.",
